{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact a5c0889fa3e08f048eb1b09057af26da62ad3882 under review request45539ee3 and my promise6567c75d, naming primary5343a64b and all nineteen exact-path companions. This reports the S1 correction review on implementation requestac54fe71/promisea4c569b1 under proposal7a71886b and Hugh adoptionba18cd1a. It neither closes parent22168 nor delivers S2/S3.\n\nArchitecture. The affected contracts are the layer6 projection interpretation and layer7 application/HTTP reporting. Layer6 gains no projected field, schema or authority rule. Layer7 extends read-only checkout reporting with the adopted association and conservative cleanup protections. Its same-head architecture, landing-observations page and two design notes accompany the implementation. The seven-file delta frome962fa7b discharges the prior predicate defect: AdviseCheckouts publishes only when !read.Exhausted() \u0026\u0026 table.Complete. Every association refusal flows through that completion flag, while the shared check covers its budget, deadline and cancellation. The table's reason is retained, with exhaustedRead only as fallback. Both candidate advice and association annotations are withheld together. handleWorktrees obtains its pair through this function; the two judgment methods remain separately callable, so this approval certifies that endpoint contract, not an absolute API restriction on every possible caller. The restriction would require an additional design choice and is not necessary to meet this request.\n\nSecurity. The changed predicate only removes advice. It clears the candidate list and each checkout's classification/grade, governing record, Row/Rows, approval, landed target and remote-containment answer when the observation is incomplete. It does not promote an unsigned claim, convert unknown into a negative, change authentication, weaken pending-decision/containment/refless protections, or write repository state. The ref inventory, tip, per-tip depth, unheld-object and cancellation failures remain conservative. My strengthened controls confirm genuinely offered and graded positive checkouts, then verify all cleared fields and matching reasons with the shared read still unexhausted for all three association-specific bounds. No unresolved security defect found. The governing proposal and Hugh's ratification are effective and unretired; this is ordinary assigned implementation under that direct adoption, not a new authority-bearing-chain adoption.\n\nSimplification. One completion conjunction covers the association's existing failure cases without duplicating their limits at the endpoint. Passing the existing reason into unknownWorktrees removes the generic-reason assumption while preserving its other callers. The shared helper and three eligible fixtures exercise the response outcome directly; no extra state, identity store, API restriction or production hook is needed. The two judgments continue sharing inputs and budget without sharing authority.\n\nValidation. Fresh independent targeted app tests under Go1.26.7 and -race pass60.775s. An owned overlay strengthens the three new subtests: it asserts the positive grade, no shared-budget/deadline exhaustion, every cleared advice field, and the common bound-specific reason; all three pass22.297s. Actual production-code omissions are killed: restoring the old predicate leaves a settled Row/LandedInto/deletable answer beside the missing-tip refusal (1.768s), and restoring the generic reason loses the missing-tip diagnosis (1.730s). These are my fresh runs. I also read the author's eight fresh gate results, including full-module/app-race/docset success, and the twenty-seven-control record; I did not independently rerun that entire suite or every historical mutant. The earlier grading, cache, captured-read and trust conclusions carry over byte-identical source outside the seven-file correction. No native-browser or resident validation is claimed.\n\nProvenance and landing. All twenty current candidates are live, effective and unflagged. I checked52 artifact-to-artifact basis edges: current-head behavior edges are distinct from historical predecessors; each historical predecessor is live, unflagged, at the same exact path and ancestral to mainc0108be8. No old S1-head or checkpoint artifact is used. The candidate app.go predates the landed oversized-attachment signing change; that fact is not erased by unflagged provenance. My clean merge-tree is8226bc079a769174fe68cea740bdde0992ed8184, and its app.go delta frommain contains only S1 reporting/cache changes, preserving the landed signing behavior. This is a merge-tree inspection, not a merged-tree test run.\n\nRatify this exact verdict, run the required landing checks on the actual merge tree, then seal with exact-path succession, push main/sequence/receipt refs, verify CI and remove the implementation worktree/branch. Preserve the S2/S3 and parent outcomes, disclosed TypeScript/wireparity scope and absence of a resident rollout. Any new implementation head requires fresh artifacts and review.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:5343a64b18dc8308a42e692e7bb9383886677005","binding":"assigned","head":"a5c0889fa3e08f048eb1b09057af26da62ad3882","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6567c75d4f4e0fd28571e6705f86bb027cbb90c0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a4c569b1cddfb0db72f9239488851f19a291906f\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:936b78362915e772e93d1450fd8068b8a8d4633b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:044bfcf29929a723ef828385a4cbf501dbad6912, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:07b4c65e9516179f7b6405f45ca72183d99f572d, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0cb256ee584ecca238d95616b